/T (In particular, since Quick, Draw! sketches are sparse, minimal, and inconsistent across users, we adopted an incremental complexity strategy. We started from a lightweight baseline and progressively introduced regularization, augmentation, automated tuning, and transfer learning to find the right model capacity without overfitting.)
/E (In particular, since Quick, Draw! sketches are sparse, minimal, and inconsistent across users, we adopted an incremental complexity strategy. We started from a lightweight baseline and progressively introduced regularization, augmentation, automated tuning, and transfer learning to find the right model capacity without overfitting.)
